keywords:
  - earthquake prediction
  - hurricane rapid intensification
  - tornado prediction
  - coherence field theory
  - Helmholtz PDE
  - natural hazard forecasting
  - ensemble machine learning
abstract: >-
  Three natural hazard prediction systems derived from a single partial
  differential equation (Helmholtz coherence PDE). Earthquake prediction
  (AUC 0.733 on 980 mainshocks, exceeding rate-only baseline by +0.137),
  hurricane rapid intensification (AUC 0.967 on IBTrACS best-track),
  and tornado formation (AUC 0.644 day-ahead with no same-day data).
  All models are pure Python + NumPy with every algorithm implemented
  from scratch. Honest methodology: temporal train/test splits, bootstrap
  confidence intervals, fair baselines on the same test set.
